 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Marijuana (cannabis, “banga”, “weed”) is an illegal drug from the leaves of the cannabis plant. It is smoked or eaten.\nEffects: poor memory and concentration, anxiety and fear, hallucinations, mental illness (psychosis), lung damage, laziness and school failure, dependence.\nTramadol is a strong painkiller that must only be taken on a doctor's prescription. Young people abuse it, sometimes mixed with energy drinks or alcohol, to feel “high” or strong.\nEffects of tramadol abuse: addiction, seizures (fits), breathing problems, and death from overdose; violence and crime.\nSocial effects of drug abuse: dropping out of school, theft, prison (selling and using marijuana are crimes), broken families.\nHelp: talk to a parent, teacher, counsellor or health worker. Refuse firmly, avoid places where drugs are used, and choose good friends and activities.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
